    {
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 35 },
      "id": 15,
      "options": {
        "content": "<h3>How to read this demo</h3><p><b>Actual node CPU</b> shows current VM work. <b>Request reservation</b> shows what Kubernetes can guarantee to a new Pod. A Worker needs <code>250m CPU + 512Mi memory</code> on one Ready worker node, so it can remain Pending even while actual node CPU is low.</p><p><b>KEDA Scale-out Requested</b> is derived from desired Worker replicas above the minimum of two. Use the ScaleCart Dashboard or <code>kubectl get scaledobject</code> for the exact KEDA Active condition.</p>",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.1.0",
      "title": "Demo Reading Guide",
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    }
